{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"partly\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"yes\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"In contrast, gait freezing was characterized by a low frequency cortical-subthalamic decoupling in the hemisphere with less striatal dopaminergic innervation (H−) (Fig. 4A).\",\n    \"We first studied power changes in low frequency (i.e. θ-α rhythms) and in the β-frequency band of the two STN and did not find any differences during gait freezing in comparison to (effective) walking (Fig. 3A and B).\",\n    \"We also assessed the duration of β-burst and did not find a difference between (effective) walking and gait freezing (Fig. 3C).\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"We first studied power changes in low frequency (i.e. θ-α rhythms) and in the β-frequency band of the two STN and did not find any differences during gait freezing in comparison to (effective) walking (Fig. 3A and B).\",\n    \"We also assessed the duration of β-burst and did not find a difference between (effective) walking and gait freezing (Fig. 3C).\",\n    \"In contrast, gait freezing was characterized by a low frequency cortical-subthalamic decoupling in the hemisphere with less striatal dopaminergic innervation (H−) (Fig. 4A).\",\n    \"Despite the lack of subthalamic activity changes during gait freezing in our study, exaggerated STN β-synchronization may still influence dynamic motor processing in favour of gait freezing development (Anidi et al., 2018).\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"报告的说法判为partly：原文明确支持冻结期间theta-alpha皮层-STN耦合下降，因此将该研究作为这一网络耦合结果的依据是正确的。但原文同时明确报告了三个局部STN阴性结果：低频（theta-alpha）功率无显著差异、beta功率无显著差异、beta burst持续时间无显著差异。如果第5.4节只呈现耦合下降而没有充分呈现这些结果，就会使研究发现的整体图景不完整，尤其可能造成将网络耦合异常与局部STN振荡异常混为一谈的问题。不过，附件没有提供报告第5.4节本身，因此无法独立核实beta冲突表的具体内容及其实际遗漏程度。指控者的说法判为yes：上述三个阴性结果均有原文直接依据，而且原文第100行附近的结果明确报告了theta-alpha皮层-STN解耦，说明两类结果确实同时存在。阴性结果限制了将局部STN beta异常视为普遍冻结机制的解释，但不能据此断言STN beta活动完全不参与冻结。原文讨论部分明确保留了这种可能性。另需注意，研究比较的是患者冻结期间与患者自身有效步行（effective walking），而不是与健康对照者的正常步行；研究仅纳入7名患者，并记录到14次冻结事件。因此，指控者的核心判断成立，但应避免将实验结果扩大为对所有冻结情境的绝对结论。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "3b409767-ab6e-4911-88cd-126f9860ea1c", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T114204056413Z", "elapsed_seconds": 122.594, "completed_utc": "2026-11-13T11:44:06.670129+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "1e5a643c99bdaf91d2c3b7e46b4a76a2f17acd6280b840119b8da21cc013bde4", "attachment_count": 1}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "Nozomi Kasaki / gpt4", "account_sha256": "bbd4fd636d4b6714d2b42b89e341bdb5bbe7c34f7d141aec76b444be8343fe54", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not_applicable_no_browser", "attachment_count": 1, "code_sha256": {"tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_cli.py": "96a4cdb6cd5d982f4d1de5b6ba8fae0cf23ee44aa3e41d7fdf6968e3fb590e48", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_sessions.py": "83a3ed4ae1efa9f1a2b8ee3f144cc0dc9f668f995a33cc4222308cb3fa31f683", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_attachments.py": "eedfa23885000025700f6306b1d1f4582896a7370734be506c156dee532fd7d7"}}, "screenshot_evidence": {"complete": true, "kind": "offline_actual_HTTP_response", "directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T114204056413Z", "files": ["proof-offline.png"], "sha256": {"proof-offline.png": "20095c806d00182998edc23b22ab53f58e56081c01b3ca42654c783cc29fdb3f"